{
 "_doc": "First-phrase gate vectors, one phone per case. See PROTOCOL.md 'Commands', The first phrase decides. role: opener = this phone opened the talk; other = it did not; solo = the host's talk has no client. atMs = when the phrase's result arrives, after this phone's live earcon; FIRST_PHRASE_MS = 8000, inclusive. expect[i] = the command text for phrases[i] (the normalisation of 'Commands' up to and including trim, before the hey/please drop), or null = conversation. A case with interpret: true is a phone whose host interprets (PROTOCOL.md 'Commands', Interpretation): the opener's first phrase is a candidate whether it parses or not, so expect is its text; without the field, interpret is false. A case with askAtMs is one where the host asks a clarifying question (PROTOCOL.md 'Commands', The clarifying question) that reaches this phone at that time, before any phrase with the same or a later atMs: the next non-empty phrase within answerMs = 10000 of it (inclusive) is the reply, passed on as it is.",
 "firstPhraseMs": 8000,
 "answerMs": 10000,
